31. Types of improvement schemes.--
An improvement scheme shall be of one of the following types or may combine any two or more of such types or of special features thereof, that is to say-
(a) a general improvement scheme;
(b) a re-building scheme;
(c) a re-housing scheme;
(d) a street scheme;
(e) a deferred street scheme;
(f) a development scheme;
(g) a housing accommodation scheme;
(h) a town expansion scheme;
(i) a drainage or drainage including sewage disposal scheme; and
(j) a playground. stadium and recreation ground scheme. Section 38. ''Housing accommodation scheme.-
Whenever the Trust is of opinion that it is expedient and for the public advantage to provide housing accommodation for any class of the inhabitants within the Trust area, the Trust may frame a housing accommodation scheme for such purpose.
